Phase 17 – Step 5: Understand and Configure csi-config-map.yaml

This is the first manifest we will apply.

What does it do?

The ConfigMap tells the Ceph CSI driver:

Which Ceph cluster to connect to
Which monitor(s) to contact

Without it, the CSI driver has no idea where your Ceph cluster is.

Think of it like this:

Kubernetes
    │
Ceph CSI
    │
❓ Where is the Ceph cluster?
    │
Reads ConfigMap
    │
FSID + Monitor IP
    │
Connects to Ceph


cat > csi-config-map.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ConfigMap
metadata:
  name: ceph-csi-config
  namespace: ceph-csi
data:
  config.json: |-
    [
      {
        "clusterID": "ab181f75-9281-11f1-8d34-0225cf85069e",
        "monitors": [
          "192.168.64.13:3300",
          "192.168.64.13:6789"
        ]
      }
    ]

 Apply: 
 	kubectl apply -f csi-config-map.yaml

 Verify:
 	kubectl get configmap -n ceph-csi


